## Goal
Make the `portero` CLI's default status/set report work for an app installed via Homebrew cask (in /Applications) as well as `make install`, and warn when the installed app is quarantined by macOS (DEV-75).

## Problems
None.

## Decision
- `installedApp()` now returns the bundle the running binary lives in, and falls back to `~/Applications/Portero.app` only for a bare CLI binary. The bundle detection was split into a testable `bundleOf(exe)`.
- A quarantine warning is printed after `default status` and `default set`. It explains Gatekeeper will block the first link and gives two fixes: Open Anyway, or `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine`. It never changes the exit status.
- The check `quarantined()` runs `/usr/bin/xattr -p com.apple.quarantine` in `quarantine_darwin.go`. Any failure counts as "not quarantined", so the check can't get in the way. A `quarantine_other.go` stub returns false on other platforms.
- Hints that said "run make install" now also mention `brew reinstall --cask portero`, and the not-in-bundle message names the cask.
- Tests cover `bundleOf`, the warning text, and `quarantined` on a temp dir (darwin only).

